    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that submits an audio file for batch transcription using a concrete external provider, I will use the AWS Transcribe service, which is a widely used and reliable provider for batch transcription. The code will include the necessary AWS SDK import and the specific service client to make the provider identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789848886945,
          "start": 1789848884965
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb4e96e5001hDe9OjdGTne3kk",
      "message_id": "msg_0bb4e913e001aP26IWZiToplFO",
      "session_id": "ses_f44b16f43ffeks9rP2OTk7wxes",
      "time_created": 1789848884965,
      "time_updated": 1789848886946
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_pEQCxuh0e23MmKHPbNdfAA",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef submit_transcription(audio_file_uri, transcription_job_name):\n    transcribe = boto3.client('transcribe')\n    response = transcribe.start_transcription_job(\n        TranscriptionJobName=transcription_job_name,\n        Media={'MediaFileUri': audio_file_uri},\n        MediaFormat='mp3',\n        LanguageCode='en-US'\n    )\n    print(response)\n\n# Example usage:\n# submit_transcription('s3://your-bucket/your-audio-file.mp3', 'my-transcription-job')",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-22w667i_/submit_transcription.py"
          },
